{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/19723-insensate-tilt-lunacy-d","id":19723,"title":"Insensate Tilt = Lunacy? :D","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-28T07:26:41-08:00","id":19723,"title":"Insensate Tilt = Lunacy? :D","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GMC pag 211</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Insensate</b><br /> The character shuts down, either due to extreme fear or sudden pleasure. He may huddle in a corner, cringe away from sudden noises, or stare into space as waves of pleasure lap over him.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> The character can\u2019t take any actions until the Tilt is resolved. He can apply Defense to incoming attacks, and if he takes any damage from an attack, he\u2019s knocked free of whatever fogged his brain.<br /> <b>Causing the Tilt:</b> Several supernatural powers can leave their victim in a trance-like state of heightened emotion, whether it\u2019s a vampire\u2019s mind-affecting tricks or the <b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">pants-shitting terror of witnessing a werewolf take on an inhuman form</span></b>. A truly heroic amount of alcohol or a hallucinogenic drug might have similar effects; administering such a drug is a Dexterity + Weaponry attack, suffering a \u22121 modifier for the improvised weapon.<br /> <b>Ending the Tilt:</b> The Tilt wears off at the end of the<br /> scene. The victim can spend a point of Willpower before then to act normally for one turn. A successful attack will also end the Tilt. If a character has been knocked insensible by drugs,<br /> this Tilt is replaced with the Drugged Tilt when it ends.</div> </div> </div> </div>Discuss. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T08:33:12-08:00","id":19758,"title":"","content":"I have a feeling it will be part of the new Lunacy rules, but not the sum total of how Lunacy works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T08:43:59-08:00","id":19762,"title":"","content":"I have the same feeling. This effect still doesn't exactly feel like the old Lunacy and doesn't achieve the same goal. Though it might be useful while we don't have clear Idigam Chronicles Rules Updates on Lunacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T11:38:56-08:00","id":19845,"title":"","content":"That doesn't work anything like lunacy. There is no running, no memory loss, and the only thing your going on is the werewolf line in the description. It basically is just what they decided to call a condition for a catatonic state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T12:10:39-08:00","id":19850,"title":"","content":"It looks like a quick-and-dirty way to treat it in the meantime, much like that honorary Rank sidebar and Renown references. I wouldn't assume it's going to stay relevant unless it's a condition inflicted due to a circumstance beyond shapeshifting in of itself (which is to say, other rolls, dramatic failures and similar). If it was tacked on as a default assumption with just a shapeshift and no other factors, I'd toss it out anyhow unless the mortal witnesses were &quot;extras&quot; anyhow.<br /> <br /> It's patently goofy in a narrative when you set up a scene to have a bunch of people shaking, pissing themselves and staring like an invalid for a scene without Willpower usage and not being inflicted pretty damn beefy power. Great for a player to feel like McBadass, but... yeah. No. Pretty goofy outside of that for something that sticks around for a scene. <br /> <br /> Now as the response to a Dramatic Failure to resisting a werewolf's Predatory Aura... that I could see as very appropriate. Just seeing one shapeshift, and then getting the Insensate Tilt in a conflict? Especially with no capacity to get out of dodge (note, it says any action at all and only brings up basic Defense) for a scene afterwards unless attacked? I'd keep this relegated to people &quot;breaking&quot; when confronted -badly- rather than automatic personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T11:24:56-08:00","id":20259,"title":"","content":"Fugue I would say is more like Lunacy as is. Its basically a memory loss+freak out anytime anything reminds you of the event.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}